---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../components/Disclaimer.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Community guidelines"
  description="How feedback is moderated on Travis Dater's project site."
>
  <article class="wrap--narrow section prose">
    <p class="eyebrow">Rules</p>
    <h1>Community guidelines</h1>
    <Disclaimer />
    <h2>What that means in practice</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Disagreement is fine.</strong> "This feature is pointless" or "1.8 broke my adapter
        and I'm annoyed" are welcome, as long as they're aimed at the software and not at a person.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Bug reports are wanted</strong>, even frustrated ones. Steps to reproduce help more
        than volume.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Deleted without discussion:</strong> harassment, slurs, threats, personal attacks,
        doxxing, spam, advertising, and anything illegal.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Review first.</strong> Public submissions appear only after review, so there can be
        a delay. Not everything gets published, and approval isn't a promise to build anything.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Private stays private.</strong> Private reports and reply emails are never
        published.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Keep secrets out.</strong> Don't post passwords, API keys, unredacted logs, VINs or
        device identifiers. Anything like that is removed.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Moderation actions</h2>
    <p>
      Travis can approve, reject, hide, mark as spam, remove, or reply to a submission. Removing
      erases the content. Details are on the <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a class="btn" href="/feedback">
        Send feedback
      </a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
